      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm trying to run this macro for my monthly reports but it keeps crashing. i keep getting \"run-time error '1004': application-defined or object-defined error\". can u help me see what's wrong?\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Reconciliation\")\n    \n    Dim lastRow As Long\n    lastRow = ws.Cells(ws.Rows.Count, \"A\").End(xlUp).Row\n    \n    For i = 2 To lastRow\n        If ws.Cells(i, 1).Value <> \"\" Then\n            ws.Range(\"B\" & i).Value = ws.Cells(i, 1).Value * 1.05\n        End If\n    Next i\n    \n    ws.Range(\"B1\").Select\nEnd Sub",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The error \"run-time error '1004'\" usually means Excel is having a hard time finding a specific object or cell, which is often because the sheet name isn't exactly what you think it is, or the range is too vague.\n\nTo fix this, you should double-check that the sheet is actually named \"Reconciliation\" (case-sensitive in Excel) and that the data starts exactly where you expect. You can also try adding error handling with `On Error Resume Next` to see if a specific cell is causing the crash, or simply ensure the `Range` object is fully qualified.\n\nHere is a slightly modified version of your code that adds a bit more robustness and prints a message if something goes wrong:\n\n```vba\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Dim lastRow As Long\n    Dim i As Long\n    \n    ' Try to set the sheet, handle if it doesn't exist\n    On Error Resume Next\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Reconciliation\")\n    If ws Is Nothing Then\n        MsgBox \"Sheet 'Reconciliation' not found! Check the name carefully.\"\n        Exit Sub\n    End If\n    On Error GoTo",
